    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands as our premier play with a standout 83.53 efficiency score. While he faces an elite-hold SP in Holmes, the combination of a favorable RHP matchup, prime #2 spot in the order, and the essential stolen base upside makes him the cornerstone of our outfield. Similarly, **Josh Naylor** (73.37) and **Mickey Moniak** (68.92) offer high-floor production; **Mickey Moniak** specifically benefits from favorable wind conditions and a strong platoon advantage against Webb, pushing his value well into the \"Strong\" start tier despite the tougher opponent. We are also leaning heavily on **Seiya Suzuki** (67.75) and **Gabriel Moreno** (66.43), both of whom take advantage of soft matchups against starters with xERAs north of 4.50.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's board was navigating the fringe starts near the 50-point threshold. **Isaac Paredes** (58.24) narrowly made the cut over **Henry Bolte** (48.54), primarily due to **Isaac Paredes**\u2019s superior lineup position at #3 compared to the #9 anchor spot for **Henry Bolte**. While **Henry Bolte** benefits from a massive park boost against a left-handed arm, the volatility of the bottom-of-the-order hitting pushed him just below our desired floor. We are keeping a close watch on **Max Muncy** (55.64) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (57.87); both are currently pending official lineup confirmation. Should either slide down in the order, their scores will degrade rapidly, potentially forcing us to look at bench depth\u2014though with **James Wood**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** all currently sidelined on the IL, and **Jose Caballero** resting, our bench flexibility is severely limited.\n\nRisks remain, particularly with the lefty-heavy matchups for **Travis Bazzana** and **Austin Riley**. **Travis Bazzana** is our most concerning start at 42.21, as the L/L platoon disadvantage against Peralta significantly dampens his output. We are effectively playing him for the volume, but he is at high risk of being a drag on our daily AVG. Across the board, we are prioritizing sprint speed and platoon leverage to maintain our edge in the steals category, but the health status of contributors like **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Edwin Arroyo** remains a constant narrative as we push through mid-August. Stay disciplined on these caps; we need every point of efficiency to secure the win.",
